SPU: the drain resume resolves through the resident code spans, like indirect dispatch and the interpreter rejoin.

A registered code region that a DMA GET loaded owns its local-store span: inside it only that image's lift may run, and a
miss there is interpreted. #481 (with #419) makes spu_lifted_lookup and spu_indirect_branch resolve that way;
the drain's resume after a call bracket still looked up the overlay and then the context's own image, so it took the
stale lift of the image underneath. Resistance 3's job dispatcher loads each job module at LS 0x100, over the policy
module (igPm, 0xA00) that started it; a resume at a pc in 0xA00 found igPm's lift there, which went back to waiting for
a signal, and the job never completed. The resume now asks spu_lifted_lookup (with its dispatch cache), which since v0.19.0
also sets ctx->reloc_delta when the pc is in relocatable code (#636).

Scripted run: boot, Continue, gameplay; jobs complete (no joblist hang).

Upstream: not proposed yet (the drain-resume gap of PR #419/#481).
